{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"tests/e2e/conftest.py","reason":"bound the two provisioning subprocess.run calls (npm install line 51, npm run build line 57) with explicit timeout= so exceeding one yields a diagnosable failure naming the provisioning step rather than an os._exit(1) worker kill; also make concurrent provisioning by multiple xdist workers safe"},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"add a pre-pytest toolchain provisioning step plus an npm cache keyed on tests/e2e/js/package-lock.json, so cold install time is not charged against a single test's 300s pytest-timeout budget"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"portable e2e-deps target (npm ci + npm run build) so the fix is not CI-only per the project.portability criterion, and the in-fixture provisioning fallback keeps working in a checkout with no CI provider"}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1788479688758205001,"uuid":"1f0d952c-91f0-4877-97e9-8182cb570df5"}